# Phase 5 — Dependency Injection (Hilt Modules)
## Objective Configure Hilt modules to provide all dependencies: Room database, Retrofit, DataStore, and repository bindings.
---
## 5.1 — DatabaseModule
**File:** `di/DatabaseModule.kt`
```kotlin package com.example.twitchtest.di
import android.content.Context import androidx.room.Room import com.example.twitchtest.data.local.AppDatabase import com.example.twitchtest.data.local.UserDao import dagger.Module import dagger.Provides import dagger.hilt.InstallIn import dagger.hilt.android.qualifiers.ApplicationContext import dagger.hilt.components.SingletonComponent import javax.inject.Singleton
@Module @InstallIn(SingletonComponent::class) object DatabaseModule {
@Provides @Singleton fun provideDatabase(@ApplicationContext context: Context): AppDatabase = Room.databaseBuilder( context, AppDatabase::class.java, "twitch_test_db" ).build()
@Provides fun provideUserDao(database: AppDatabase): UserDao = database.userDao() } ```
---
## 5.2 — NetworkModule
**File:** `di/NetworkModule.kt`
```kotlin package com.example.twitchtest.di
import com.example.twitchtest.data.remote.RandomUserApiService import dagger.Module import dagger.Provides import dagger.hilt.InstallIn import dagger.hilt.components.SingletonComponent import okhttp3.OkHttpClient import okhttp3.logging.HttpLoggingInterceptor import retrofit2.Retrofit import retrofit2.converter.gson.GsonConverterFactory import javax.inject.Singleton
@Module @InstallIn(SingletonComponent::class) object NetworkModule {
private const val BASE_URL = "https://randomuser.me/"
@Provides @Singleton fun provideOkHttpClient(): OkHttpClient = OkHttpClient.Builder() .addInterceptor( HttpLoggingInterceptor().apply { level = HttpLoggingInterceptor.Level.BODY } ) .build()
@Provides @Singleton fun provideRetrofit(okHttpClient: OkHttpClient): Retrofit = Retrofit.Builder() .baseUrl(BASE_URL) .client(okHttpClient) .addConverterFactory(GsonConverterFactory.create()) .build()
@Provides @Singleton fun provideRandomUserApiService(retrofit: Retrofit): RandomUserApiService = retrofit.create(RandomUserApiService::class.java) } ```
---
## 5.3 — DataStoreModule
**File:** `di/DataStoreModule.kt`
```kotlin package com.example.twitchtest.di
import android.content.Context import androidx.datastore.core.DataStore import androidx.datastore.preferences.core.Preferences import com.example.twitchtest.data.local.dataStore import dagger.Module import dagger.Provides import dagger.hilt.InstallIn import dagger.hilt.android.qualifiers.ApplicationContext import dagger.hilt.components.SingletonComponent import javax.inject.Singleton
@Module @InstallIn(SingletonComponent::class) object DataStoreModule {
@Provides @Singleton fun provideDataStore(@ApplicationContext context: Context): DataStore<Preferences> = context.dataStore } ```
---
## 5.4 — RepositoryModule
**File:** `di/RepositoryModule.kt`
```kotlin package com.example.twitchtest.di
import com.example.twitchtest.data.repository.StreamKeyRepositoryImpl import com.example.twitchtest.data.repository.UserRepositoryImpl import com.example.twitchtest.domain.repository.StreamKeyRepository import com.example.twitchtest.domain.repository.UserRepository import dagger.Binds import dagger.Module import dagger.hilt.InstallIn import dagger.hilt.components.SingletonComponent import javax.inject.Singleton
@Module @InstallIn(SingletonComponent::class) abstract class RepositoryModule {
@Binds @Singleton abstract fun bindUserRepository( impl: UserRepositoryImpl ): UserRepository
@Binds @Singleton abstract fun bindStreamKeyRepository( impl: StreamKeyRepositoryImpl ): StreamKeyRepository } ```
---
## Design Notes
- **`@InstallIn(SingletonComponent::class)`** — All modules live for the app lifetime. - **`@Binds`** is used in `RepositoryModule` because we're binding interfaces to implementations (more efficient than `@Provides`). - **`@Provides`** is used for third-party classes (Room, Retrofit, OkHttp, DataStore). - **`StreamManager`** does not need a module — it uses `@Inject constructor` + `@Singleton` directly. - Use cases don't need modules either — they use `@Inject constructor`.
---
## Dependency Graph
``` ViewModel └── UseCase (@Inject) └── Repository (interface, bound via @Binds) ├── UserDao (provided by DatabaseModule) ├── RandomUserApiService (provided by NetworkModule) └── DataStore (provided by DataStoreModule) ```
---
## Checklist
- [ ] `DatabaseModule` provides `AppDatabase` and `UserDao` - [ ] `NetworkModule` provides `OkHttpClient`, `Retrofit`, and `RandomUserApiService` - [ ] `DataStoreModule` provides `DataStore<Preferences>` - [ ] `RepositoryModule` binds `UserRepository` and `StreamKeyRepository` - [ ] All modules annotated with `@Module`, `@InstallIn(SingletonComponent::class)` - [ ] Singletons annotated with `@Singleton` - [ ] Project compiles with Hilt annotation processing (KSP)

# Phase 7 — Permissions & Polish

## Objective
Handle runtime permissions for Camera and Microphone, manage lifecycle properly, and handle edge cases.

---

## 7.1 — Runtime Permission Handling

Permissions must be requested at runtime on Android 6.0+ (our minSdk is 29).

### Permission Utility Composable

**File:** `presentation/common/PermissionHandler.kt`

```kotlin
package com.example.twitchtest.presentation.common

import android.Manifest
import androidx.activity.compose.rememberLauncherForActivityResult
import androidx.activity.result.contract.ActivityResultContracts
import androidx.compose.runtime.*

@Composable
fun RequestStreamingPermissions(
    onAllGranted: () -> Unit,
    onDenied: () -> Unit
) {
    val permissions = arrayOf(
        Manifest.permission.CAMERA,
        Manifest.permission.RECORD_AUDIO
    )

    val launcher = rememberLauncherForActivityResult(
        ActivityResultContracts.RequestMultiplePermissions()
    ) { results ->
        if (results.values.all { it }) {
            onAllGranted()
        } else {
            onDenied()
        }
    }

    LaunchedEffect(Unit) {
        launcher.launch(permissions)
    }
}
```

### Integration in `MainStreamScreen`

Wrap the main content with permission check:

```kotlin
@Composable
fun MainStreamScreen(viewModel: MainStreamViewModel = hiltViewModel()) {
    var permissionsGranted by remember { mutableStateOf(false) }
    var permissionsDenied by remember { mutableStateOf(false) }

    if (!permissionsGranted && !permissionsDenied) {
        RequestStreamingPermissions(
            onAllGranted = { permissionsGranted = true },
            onDenied = { permissionsDenied = true }
        )
    }

    if (permissionsDenied) {
        // Show a message asking user to grant permissions in settings
        Box(Modifier.fillMaxSize(), contentAlignment = Alignment.Center) {
            Text("Camera and Microphone permissions are required for streaming.")
        }
        return
    }

    if (!permissionsGranted) return

    // ... existing MainStreamScreen content (camera preview, controls, etc.)
}
```

---

## 7.2 — Lifecycle Management

### Stop Stream on Activity Destroy

In `MainStreamViewModel.onCleared()`, `StreamManager.release()` is already called.

### Handle App Backgrounding

Add a `DisposableEffect` in `MainStreamScreen` to handle lifecycle:

```kotlin
val lifecycleOwner = LocalLifecycleOwner.current
DisposableEffect(lifecycleOwner) {
    val observer = LifecycleEventObserver { _, event ->
        when (event) {
            Lifecycle.Event.ON_PAUSE -> {
                // Optionally pause preview (stream keeps running)
            }
            Lifecycle.Event.ON_RESUME -> {
                // Resume preview if needed
            }
            Lifecycle.Event.ON_DESTROY -> {
                viewModel.getStreamManager().release()
            }
            else -> {}
        }
    }
    lifecycleOwner.lifecycle.addObserver(observer)
    onDispose {
        lifecycleOwner.lifecycle.removeObserver(observer)
    }
}
```

---

## 7.3 — Error Handling

### Stream Connection Errors

The `StreamManager` already updates `StreamStatus` to `OFFLINE` on connection failure via `ConnectChecker.onConnectionFailed()`.

Optionally, expose an error message:

```kotlin
// In StreamManager
private val _errorMessage = MutableSharedFlow<String>()
val errorMessage: SharedFlow<String> = _errorMessage.asSharedFlow()

override fun onConnectionFailed(reason: String) {
    _streamStatus.value = StreamStatus.OFFLINE
    stopTimer()
    scope.launch { _errorMessage.emit(reason) }
}

override fun onAuthError() {
    _streamStatus.value = StreamStatus.OFFLINE
    stopTimer()
    scope.launch { _errorMessage.emit("Authentication failed. Check your stream key.") }
}
```

Show as a `Snackbar` in `MainStreamScreen`:

```kotlin
val snackbarHostState = remember { SnackbarHostState() }

LaunchedEffect(Unit) {
    viewModel.getStreamManager().errorMessage.collect { message ->
        snackbarHostState.showSnackbar(message)
    }
}
```

### Network Error on Viewer API

Already handled in `ViewerListViewModel.loadViewers()` with try-catch. The error is displayed in the bottom sheet.

---

## 7.4 — UI Polish

### Keep Screen On During Streaming

```kotlin
val context = LocalContext.current
LaunchedEffect(state.streamStatus) {
    val activity = context as? Activity
    if (state.streamStatus == StreamStatus.ONLINE) {
        activity?.window?.addFlags(WindowManager.LayoutParams.FLAG_KEEP_SCREEN_ON)
    } else {
        activity?.window?.clearFlags(WindowManager.LayoutParams.FLAG_KEEP_SCREEN_ON)
    }
}
```

### Status Bar Styling

Already using `enableEdgeToEdge()` in `MainActivity`, which handles edge-to-edge display.

---

